* HSPICE template, NOT an executable bitcell model and NOT a foundry library.
* Supply these local includes. Both cell and gate must use the same process corner.
.include 'LOCAL_PROCESS_MODELS.sp'
.include 'LOCAL_CELL_ADAPTERS.sp'
.option post=2
.param VCORE=1.08 CL=2f WB=0
VM vm 0 'VCORE'
VL vl 0 'VCORE'
* Initialization: write WB for 2 ns, then retain with WL low.
VBL bl 0 'WB*VCORE'
VBB bb 0 '(1-WB)*VCORE'
VWL wl 0 PULSE(0 'VCORE' 1n 50p 50p 2n 1u)
* The adapter MUST expose real storage nodes q/qb. Do not replace them by sources.
XMEM bl bb wl q qb vm 0 CIM_BITCELL
* Nearby random bit, 100 MHz, 50% duty; sweep activity separately.
VSNG s 0 PULSE(0 'VCORE' 20n 100p 100p 5n 10n)
* Compare this loaded deck against deleting XAND, XBUF and COUT (unloaded cell).
* CIM_AND2 and CIM_BUF are actual transistor-level library-cell adapters.
XAND q s p vl 0 CIM_AND2
XBUF p y vl 0 CIM_BUF
COUT y 0 'CL'
.tran 10p 220n
.measure tran PMEM AVG par('-v(vm)*i(VM)') FROM=40n TO=200n
.measure tran PLOGIC AVG par('-v(vl)*i(VL)') FROM=40n TO=200n
.measure tran QMIN MIN v(q) FROM=40n TO=200n
.measure tran QMAX MAX v(q) FROM=40n TO=200n
.measure tran QBMIN MIN v(qb) FROM=40n TO=200n
.measure tran QBMAX MAX v(qb) FROM=40n TO=200n
* For WB=1 only: SNG->output propagation. WB=0 has no rising output.
* .measure tran TD TRIG v(s) VAL='VCORE/2' RISE=5 TARG v(y) VAL='VCORE/2' RISE=5
.end
